rnationally when we think about a  trade war I think it's really useful to  think of it as a tax war right it's a  tax skirmish and the tax kermis that's  going on right now between the US and  China is a little bit like two kids who  sort of go underwater to test who can  hold their breath along yes right  because what you're really doing in a  trade war is punishing yourself you were  taxing your own companies your own  consumers and essentially saying how  long can we hold out until my opponent  changes the strategy but here's the  problem with going into a trade war with  China China can hold its breath longer  than anybody  right this is a socialist market-based  economy with unelected leaders who don't  have midterms in five months who can  basically subsidize their industries ad  infinitum and under are under no  pressure to change their strategy in the  short term so we've picked the wrong kid  to go into a you know breath-holding  contest against knowledge and China  certainly is ratcheting up its rhetoric  saying that the Trump administration is  a gang of hoodlums talk to us Derek a  little bit about how these tariffs can  potentially backfire  you mentioned harley-davidson China of  course you know if it were to put  tariffs on tech companies you know that  could really hurt you know American  companies but also a lot of companies  produce their products like iPhones in  China so it's also interconnected  explain that to us about so you know  there have been nine own goals in the  World Cup so far this summer that's the  highest in tournament history this is  the tenth own bowl of the Sun even the  US didn't enter the tournament we still  valuators have an own goal  um 87 percent of the computer companies  in China that are subject to this tariff  are non Chinese and a lot of them are  American of the 30 districts that are  most affected by the soybean tariffs  that China is now implemented on the US  25 of them voted for Donald Trump this  is a self-inf